Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Summary", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493200339967*^9, 3.985493203021244*^9}, 
   3.9854934286764593`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"c5df36d0-5c10-46ef-8374-\
1f3ca0b22e17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We consider a fixed frequency window defined by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"6.1", "\[LessEqual]", "p", "\[LessEqual]", "15", " "}], 
   TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dc36e74-20d2-4b1f-b0cd-c7fbbbd798d3"],
 "and a range of mass ratios ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "9"}]], "<=", "\[Epsilon]", "<=", "1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "6aa27eaa-f433-4c51-b3f9-441c2df3d7e9"],
 ". The main conclusions are:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9854932054463577`*^9, 3.985493293833085*^9}, {
  3.98549343486347*^9, 
  3.985493435332972*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"46b1cdf7-21e0-4d2e-8e1f-\
eb1baec35edd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The current 0PA flux data grid is more than adequate.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " With a grid of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"6.1", "\[LessEqual]", "p", "\[LessEqual]", "30"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "125ee8e2-5e91-4259-8318-d4d7f06a94fd"],
 " in steps of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0.1", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "452d1a17-a1d6-46f8-8674-122a7a5f1511"],
 ", the leading PN scaling factored out and 8th order interpolation, it \
yields an interpolated model with errors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LessTilde]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "10"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "1fd8c5ce-0c3d-4f71-b8d3-5e13548ee315"],
 ", with the worst case close to the ISCO. A grid with half as many points is \
about two orders of magnitude less accurate, as expected since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["2", "8"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"256", "\[TildeEqual]", 
     SuperscriptBox["10", "2"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "1435820c-d540-4395-8c38-1042c353802c"],
 "."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.985493381719946*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"87f4d601-c96c-453b-b583-\
6e006c51eea6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The dephasing from interpolation error is tiny.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Over an inspiral from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", "=", "15"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "30be0b1b-3d43-4b21-9a06-3312ab832cf7"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", "=", "6.1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "56492b05-148f-48e9-9eae-76cd4be4ae2a"],
 " the dephasing is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LessTilde]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "5"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "21f34082-80a1-4e85-9c45-2cba534a3b58"],
 " radians for mass ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", "=", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "6"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "15bd20a7-fcba-4de2-ad39-39cd3593c9e9"],
 ". The dephasing is dominated by the near-ISCO part, so it gets worse for \
smaller \[Epsilon] and better for larger \[Epsilon]."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.9854934587282057`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4ec4f3e2-6c7e-4e77-9349-\
25c3bb29f9ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the default options for NIntegrate the ",
 StyleBox["dephasing is dominated by integration error",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". Over a fixed frequency interval ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"6.1", "\[LessEqual]", "p", "\[LessEqual]", "15"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8c763a63-05c1-4324-98ca-325af05cf1c9"],
 "  the dephasing is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"~", 
     SuperscriptBox["10", 
      RowBox[{"-", "5"}]]}], "/", "\[Epsilon]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "fff79032-9caa-4458-b0f7-377a9b50ccca"],
 ", so for mass ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "5"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "560fe3dd-6bac-49e8-803f-ba1befd43fae"],
 " the phase error is order unity."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.985493511857772*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cac3f013-a216-4673-ad77-\
5fe1adf9fc23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Setting PrecisionGoal\[Rule]\[Infinity] helps a bit in some cases, \
but is not the best solution",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". Keep in mind the definition from Mathematica\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
documentation: \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]With PrecisionGoal->p and \
AccuracyGoal->a, the Wolfram Language attempts to make the numerical error in \
a result of size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "1825d298-a3a5-4da2-9158-57c541845442"],
 " be less than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["10", 
      RowBox[{"-", "a"}]], "+"}], "|", "x", "|", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "p"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "7356b8cf-72b9-4174-a6b4-fb799d3f7429"],
 ".\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] This means that for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "~", "1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de0c98b-d316-430d-bd91-3bf377593de0"],
 "$, PrecisionGoal and AccuracyGoal have the same effect. For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "\[GreaterGreater]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "6516e342-51a0-4fce-ad96-8a5f69682f00"],
 " the error is mostly controlled by PrecisionGoal and for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "\[LessLess]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "777fda9a-17e1-4bc0-bab1-ec6ba36605ac"],
 " the error is mostly controlled by AccuracyGoal.  The accumulated phase \
over a fixed frequency interval is large ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"~", "1"}], "/", "\[Epsilon]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "c07d04f0-d4e0-440c-80c5-aec6ead83e05"],
 " so it is true that PrecisionGoal is controlling the error tolerance. With \
PrecisionGoal\[Rule]\[Infinity] we have an absolute error tolerance of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"~", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "f42f7b7c-4029-47a0-8b74-861c6d4fb46e"],
 " (the default value for AccuracyGoal is WorkingPrecision/2), so we are \
asking for a phase with relative error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}]], "\[Epsilon]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "03a73e7b-2d6b-4b5e-89a9-76e398cbf34b"],
 ". For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", "\[LessTilde]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "7"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "f7eb1d49-088d-4a71-9949-8e087fa6cf67"],
 " this means we would need to work at greater than machine precision to \
reach the AccuracyGoal. With Mathematica, this causes it to stop integrating \
early, once the AccuracyGoal can no longer be met."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.98549373543887*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1e9f3ee6-ab11-472e-a6fc-\
7cb802d761f0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "There are ",
 StyleBox["two",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " problems with accuracy of the numerical integration:"
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.985493750418692*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"91ddc4ff-2e69-4721-a90b-\
69cf37375fc4"],

Cell["\<\
Because of point 3 above, our dephasing is above tolerance (1 radian) for \
typical EMRI mass ratios.\
\>", "SubitemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.9854937662464533`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b18098b4-0852-402a-ae28-\
40b6ec15817f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because point 4 above we can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t go below a certain mass \
ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", "\[LessTilde]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "7"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "cee0583b-0a88-49a5-84a2-a06544d5ec4d"],
 "."
}], "SubitemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.98549378556332*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e648fa20-fdcb-4bcc-b775-\
a773964c3a6d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["We can resolve these with two small tweaks:", "ItemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.985493795518425*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e4b62293-b923-4331-9946-\
2258d2374012"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Rescale the phase",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " by \[Epsilon], i.e. solve for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", " ", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "p"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8818a44d-97bf-4d67-8461-d91ebaecaf6d"],
 ". This causes the rescaled phase the be \[ScriptCapitalO](1) independently \
of mass ratio, the same as the other evolved variables (\[CapitalOmega]). \
This change ",
 StyleBox["allows us to reach smaller mass ratios",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " without Mathematica aborting the integration early. I think this is \
similar to, but not quite the same as integrating with respect to slow time."
}], "SubitemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.985493851388516*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3c68b480-1c69-4e1d-935f-\
4cba2fba7884"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use  a higher-than-default setting for PrecisionGoal ",
 StyleBox["and",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " AccuracyGoal. With both set to 12, we find a phase accuracy of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}]], "/", "\[Epsilon]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "f246551e-720f-4f13-84e9-2d707c055e21"],
 ", which should be enough for LISA EMRIs. Higher mass ratios will have \
significant phase error, but they should also involve unreasonably long \
waveforms that we will never want in actual analysis."
}], "SubitemNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985493306262289*^9, 
  3.985493877524557*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0fa6c665-db6e-418e-bf0a-\
8847794e8438"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
So, in summary, if we use our current  0PA data with the right interpolation \
and the right integration settings, then everything at 0PA should meet \
requirements. (Note that this is pretty close  to the settings we used in the \
waveform letter, a little more accurate but not too much.) There\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s no reason to expect new issues related to integration \
error to arise once we include 1PA, spin effects, etc.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9854934402063713`*^9, {3.9854938924853077`*^9, 
   3.985493894065358*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f7933aec-5184-4721-a7a3-\
54040df21582"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Load data", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985333315906748*^9, 
  3.985333317369525*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0e854573-25b9-4488-909f-\
597cc72cd39e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["First order fluxes", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.79715697342671*^9, 3.797156978826098*^9}, {
  3.797167119670039*^9, 3.797167120821348*^9}, {3.834242549091378*^9, 
  3.834242549261044*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4e07f168-f679-4865-b975-\
3e7d8561fa91"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Load data", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985324833224429*^9, 
  3.985324834238509*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ce601c64-9f1a-460a-8aef-\
2917ae066625"],

Cell["\<\
Load fluxes. These were computed by summing up to l=30, which should be \
enough to be accurate to machine precision down to the ISCO.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8486543860919456`*^9, 3.8486544261193733`*^9}, {
  3.848654492535098*^9, 3.8486544947405853`*^9}, {3.985494680908098*^9, 
  3.985494709394762*^9}, {3.985494805381563*^9, 3.985494806292098*^9}, {
  3.985572316854604*^9, 
  3.985572322319517*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9563141e-17a6-4332-add7-\
bcef01bb6f36"],

